Compiling a nullable generic override with memory-safety rules V2 could crash while override matching inspected a return type that had not yet been bound.

- **Override matching:** Treat an uninitialized return type as not an exact match, allowing the existing fallback comparer to continue matching.
- **Regression coverage:** Exercise both memory-safety rule versions with:
  ```csharp
  abstract class Base { public abstract Task<T?> M<T>(); }
  sealed class Derived : Base
  {
      public override Task<T?> M<T>() where T : default => null!;
  }
  ```

